= Test set — Simple =

A '''test set''' is data saved for evaluating a machine-learning system after its main design choices are finished.

The model should not train on the test examples.

Developers also should not keep changing the model every time they see the test score.

If they do, the test set becomes part of development and the score can become too optimistic.

A test score also does not guarantee the model will work if real-world data later change.

